      "id": "feedback-one",
      "title": "feedback, item one",
      "voiceover": {
        "text": "Telehealth attacks distance for reviews. But it can't help when someone needs an examination or a procedure, and it needs a good connection, often weakest where need is greatest. The subsidy attacks cost. But repaid after the trip, it still needs money up front, so it helps least the people with least. The classic mistake is naming the benefit and stopping there."
